    "severity": "moderate",
    "reachable": "no",
    "assessment": "npm audit emits the affected uuid leaf path plus derived paths that enter it through Expo's xcode configuration tooling. Eleven signatures rooted at direct mobile/runtime dependencies are conservatively classified across Android, web, production, and iOS build tooling, including expo-sharing's config-plugin path; the remaining eight signatures are iOS build tooling only. The affected UUID call remains in iOS configuration code rather than the Android or web application runtime. 2026-10-17 recheck: uuid 7.0.3 at node_modules/uuid is required by xcode 3.0.1 (^7.0.3). Fixed uuid 11.1.1 is a major jump. The reviewed xcode lib/pbxProject.js generateUuid uses uuid.v4() with no output buffer; advisory v3/v5/v6 buffer entry points do not match this call. Keep iOS outside the release scope; do not force a global uuid override.",
    "mitigation": "Phase 1 excludes the affected iOS configuration path; this scope boundary limits current reachability but is not a dependency fix.",
    "owner": "StrandCue maintainer",
    "approvedOn": "2026-10-06",
    "reviewOn": "2026-10-24",
    "expiresOn": "2026-10-31",
    "upgradePath": "Upgrade Expo's xcode tooling to a compatible release using a fixed uuid version, then remove this exception. Recheck published fixes on 2026-10-24; this residual expires 2026-10-31. No npm audit fix --force or incompatible Expo downgrade is permitted."
