    "severity": "high",
    "reachable": "no",
    "scope": "expo-build-tooling",
    "assessment": "The affected braces parser is present only in Metro and Expo CLI dependency paths used while building or bundling; application source does not import it and the signed APK contains no Node package tree. 2026-10-17 recheck: braces 3.0.3 at node_modules/braces is still the latest published release and is affected; no upstream fixed version exists. micromatch 4.0.8/Metro consumes braces from trusted repository/build patterns. Repeated/deeply nested hostile glob patterns can exhaust the build process stack. Controlled CI and trusted patterns are compensating controls, not a fix.",
    "mitigation": "Keep build inputs and configuration trusted, run builds in controlled CI, and reject any observed Android, web, production, mixed, or newly introduced dependency path.",
    "owner": "StrandCue maintainer",
    "approvedOn": "2026-10-06",
    "reviewOn": "2026-10-24",
    "expiresOn": "2026-10-31",
    "upgradePath": "Upgrade Expo, React Native, or Metro when their compatible dependency graph removes the affected braces release, then remove this exception. Recheck published fixes on 2026-10-24; this residual expires 2026-10-31. No npm audit fix --force or incompatible Expo downgrade is permitted."
